(globalThis.CATALOGUE_RECORD_CHUNKS??=Object.create(null))[32]={"source_order":32,"notes":["The faint marks at about x 2640–2900 may be show-through from the recto tick column or very faint direct pencil marks. They are treated as unattached and not as entries.","Show-through text was not transcribed because it is mirrored writing from fol. 16.","The gutter lies at about x≈3110–3140 native. To its right are fragments of the facing fol. 17: check marks and the shelfmark prefixes '√d. 15…', 'e.', 'f.', 'c.', and 'd.'. There are also pencil braces and an arrow, and the marginal note 'see Viveka…'. These belong to fol. 17 and are not recorded as target-page blocks.","The pencil brace and arrow between x≈3270 and 3460 lie right of the gutter. They are taken to belong to the fol. 17 margin.","The image review finds that fol. 16b is a ruled verso with no catalogue entries. Apart from the folio number '16b', no direct writing is securely identifiable.","Faint mirrored show-through of the recto (fol. 16) catalogue text is visible across the ruled lines and was not transcribed.","Faint slanted strokes resembling 'a/?' appear at about [2640,3800,160,170]. They correspond in position to the mirrored recto marginal note at about the same height, so they are judged to be show-through and are not recorded as target text.","A very faint 'd'-like or tick-like mark appears at about [2820,700,80,120]. It is probably show-through from the recto shelfmark and tick column and is not recorded.","A binding thread with a knot runs along the gutter at about x 3080–3160. This is not writing.","Right of the gutter (x>~3140) are fragments of the facing fol. 17. These include ticks, shelfmark prefixes such as 'd. 15', 'e.', 'f.', 'c.' and 'd.', pencil braces and an arrow, and the marginal note 'see Viveka…'. They belong to fol. 17 and are not recorded here.","It is not established whether the faint '?' mark (r002) is direct writing on fol. 16b or show-through from fol. 16.","It is not established whether the '?'-like mark is direct pencil writing on fol. 16b or show-through of a tick or mark from fol. 16. The exact reading is also uncertain.","Faint slanted strokes resembling 'ā/?' are at about native [2640,3810,140,130]. They are treated as show-through in the candidate's page annotations and are not recorded. This is inconsistent with recording the similar faint '?' at b901: both carry the same doubt, and either could be a direct query mark.","Small dark specks are not mentioned by the candidate or the inventory. They are at about native [425,2540,130,40] and [470,2975,90,80] in the left part of the page, and at [1180,4335,110,30] near the bottom. They look like ink or dust specks or scan debris rather than writing, but this was not confirmed."],"records":[{"id":"css-prod-0032-r001","local_id":"r001","source_order":32,"folio":"16b","folio_label":"fol. 16b","sequence":1,"page_id":"dab24ca9-ef6d-41e0-967f-1f1bd697e9d5","kind":"other","record_type":"non_catalogue_text","source_model_record_type":"non_catalogue_text","subtype":"folio_number","shelfmark":"","titleLiteral":"","titleNormalized":"","displayTitle":"Catalogue text","authorOrSource":"","source":"","subject":"","subjectGroup":"","date":"","extent":"","lines":"","script":"","incipit":"","transcription":"16b","annotations":["Ink folio number in the top left corner. The 'b' is written superscript, above and to the right of '16'."],"uncertainties":["Faint slanted strokes resembling 'ā/?' are at about native [2640,3810,140,130]. They are treated as show-through in the candidate's page annotations and are not recorded. This is inconsistent with recording the similar faint '?' at b901: both carry the same doubt, and either could be a direct query mark.","Small dark specks are not mentioned by the candidate or the inventory. They are at about native [425,2540,130,40] and [470,2975,90,80] in the left part of the page, and at [1180,4335,110,30] near the bottom. They look like ink or dust specks or scan debris rather than writing, but this was not confirmed."],"focused_readings":[],"reviewNotes":[],"editorialNotes":[],"relationships":[],"editorial_context":[],"block_ids":["b001"],"locations":[{"block_id":"b001","bbox":[355,330,130,100]}],"isCancelled":false,"needsReview":true,"human_verified":false,"verification_status":"machine_reviewed","change_audit":[],"sourceCitationURL":"https://iiif.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/iiif/canvas/dab24ca9-ef6d-41e0-967f-1f1bd697e9d5.json","auditPath":"audit/pages/0032.json","attachedNotes":[],"resolvedRelationships":[],"attachedRecords":[]},{"id":"css-prod-0032-r002","local_id":"r002","source_order":32,"folio":"16b","folio_label":"fol. 16b","sequence":2,"page_id":"dab24ca9-ef6d-41e0-967f-1f1bd697e9d5","kind":"note","record_type":"unattached_annotation","source_model_record_type":"unattached_annotation","subtype":"faint_mark","shelfmark":"","titleLiteral":"","titleNormalized":"","displayTitle":"Unattached annotation","authorOrSource":"","source":"","subject":"","subjectGroup":"","date":"","extent":"","lines":"","script":"","incipit":"","transcription":"?","annotations":["A small faint pencil-like mark resembling '?' or '2' in the lower right part of the page, between ruled lines. It sits near the position where the mirrored left-margin tick and shelfmark column of the recto (fol. 16) would show through."],"uncertainties":["It is uncertain whether this mark was written directly on fol. 16b or is show-through from fol. 16. The reading '?' versus '2' is also uncertain. It is not attachable to any entry.","It is not established whether the '?'-like mark is direct pencil writing on fol. 16b or show-through of a tick or mark from fol. 16. The exact reading is also uncertain.","Faint slanted strokes resembling 'ā/?' are at about native [2640,3810,140,130]. They are treated as show-through in the candidate's page annotations and are not recorded. This is inconsistent with recording the similar faint '?' at b901: both carry the same doubt, and either could be a direct query mark.","Small dark specks are not mentioned by the candidate or the inventory. They are at about native [425,2540,130,40] and [470,2975,90,80] in the left part of the page, and at [1180,4335,110,30] near the bottom. They look like ink or dust specks or scan debris rather than writing, but this was not confirmed."],"focused_readings":[],"reviewNotes":[],"editorialNotes":[],"relationships":[],"editorial_context":[],"block_ids":["b901"],"locations":[{"block_id":"b901","bbox":[2720,3580,60,80]}],"isCancelled":false,"needsReview":true,"human_verified":false,"verification_status":"machine_reviewed","change_audit":[],"sourceCitationURL":"https://iiif.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/iiif/canvas/dab24ca9-ef6d-41e0-967f-1f1bd697e9d5.json","auditPath":"audit/pages/0032.json","attachedNotes":[],"resolvedRelationships":[],"attachedRecords":[]}]};
